<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (The central conceptual tension in this business case is the apparent conflict between automation and luxury hospitality. Project EVT Evolution resolves this tension through a precedent-validated insight: automation does not devalue a premium brand; it elevates it by removing administrative burden from the guest journey and redirecting human attention toward emotionally resonant interactions.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (QC Terme demonstrates this explicitly, leveraging technology to enhance rather than replace the luxury experience, maintaining prestigious brand associations with Dyson and Marshall while deploying digital check-in systems. CitizenM similarly proves that digital efficiency and high-end hospitality are structurally compatible. For an international operator like EVT, automation also enables cultural adaptability: Western guests benefit from frictionless self-service efficiency, while Asian markets, particularly China, where QR-code ecosystems via Alipay and WeChat are standard, perceive technology integration as a hallmark of modern premium service rather than a cost-cutting signal.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
